  "assumptions": [
    "Charge the incoming transition through each original request-producing wave only. Give it the greatest active receiving rank saving, full exposure and zero replacement cost for the named devices; keep score reductions, five W1/W2, all slot writes, collectives and the rest of the model. Applies to the observed schedule. The extra inclusive case grants the final outgoing seed/ID costs once.",
    "Count budget is the entire original causal time from target selection to side-stream count record, including transfer; score publication, count D2H, valid/discard fallback, raw negative IDs, prepared backup and CPU reader remain obligations. ID times are only INT32→INT64 casts, Bx6 ID bank stores and predecessor slices. No wide score-bank Slice/ViewCopy is charged. Next-state ID patch and corrected-position/seq are the old disjoint motifs.",
    "Host budget exists only for matched unchanged B4 graph transitions with all four continuing, five drafts each, using the 48 archived CPU-owner samples, same two replacement dispatches. State wrapper dispatch precedes the count wait on the worker main thread. Pending wait absorbs earlier dispatch. All compatible waits are considered. No identity is inferred from absent event handles.",
    "The wave-local device-minus-host offset upper bound gives the earliest possible count-ready time. Grant all seed savings first, then cap additional main gain by min(H,max(0,wait_start-(earliest_ready-seed_credit))). Missing compatible observations retain full H. The separate enqueue-thread variant grants full H unless visible dispatch silence before every compatible return can absorb H. This assumes silence represents queue slack; otherwise use the uncapped sensitivity. The extra 0.25 ms clock allowance is a separate scenario.",
    "Summing device and residual host terms on the same rank grants serial exposure, not a measured speedup. Unsampled ordinary and changed-population host times remain unknown. B1 uses its maximum across eight ranks of one prompt-to-verification group, then the maximum of one verification-to-verification group for remaining steps. Raw-ID and cleanup extensions are sensitivities: 72 separate five-task raw signatures, same B/D or the largest archived when missing, plus matched cleanup tasks. All can be free only if the early raw IDs and the cleaned padded prefix are both produced legally. No B4 host proxy is transferred. CPU-only, ragged, PP, reordered owners, alternative sampling and state-retirement paths retain their original contracts."
